Hi Romina,

>From your output, I see that you ran codex with 5 samples from the 1000 GP. The largest K that can be set here is 5 (the number of latent factors estimated by codex, which can not exceed the number of the samples or the number of exons). This is why you got an error when K=6.

Also, to gain better performance, I would suggest at least 20-30 samples to be processed together. We’ve analyzed bam file from different batches so it’s not required that they come from a homogeneous sample pool.

Hope that this helps,
Yuchao

>
